igure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/04\/DSC_1973.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"In 1506, Pope Julius II commissioned Bramante to rebuild the church into what it is today. In the mid-1600s, Bernini created the columned wings of the square. They are intended to create a welcoming environment and welcome both believers and non-believers alike. The church was finally completed in 1626.\" data-attachment-id=\"1457\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"In 1506, Pope Julius II commissioned Bramante to rebuild the church into what it is today. In the mid-1600s, Bernini created the columned wings of the square. They are intended to create a welcoming environment and welcome both believers and non-believers alike. The church was finally completed in 1626.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2017\/04\/DSC_1973\/815995913.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">In 1506, Pope Julius II commissioned Bramante to rebuild the church into what it is today. In the mid-1600s, Bernini created the columned wings of the square. They are intended to create a welcoming environment and welcome both believers and non-believers alike. The church was finally completed in 1626.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/04\/DSC_1941.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The oval courtyard is the site of Nero\u2019s Roman chariot racecourse. At halftime, Romans killed Christians for entertainment. Whether forcing them to fight with wild animals or gladiators or being crucified, Romans always came up with creative ways to kill the religious minority. It is believed that Peter was also killed during these halftimes around 65 A.D. and later laid to rest in the cemetery on the Vatican Hill. Emperor Constantinople ordered a church to be built over Peter\u2019s remains in 320. Peter is considered the first pope.\" data-attachment-id=\"1451\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The oval courtyard is the site of Nero\u2019s Roman chariot racecourse. At halftime, Romans killed Christians for entertainment. Whether forcing them to fight with wild animals or gladiators or being crucified, Romans always came up with creative ways to kill the religious minority. It is believed that Peter was also killed during these halftimes around 65 A.D. and later laid to rest in the cemetery on the Vatican Hill. Emperor Constantinople ordered a church to be built over Peter\u2019s remains in 320. Peter is considered the first pope.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2017\/04\/DSC_1941\/556947075.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">The oval courtyard is the site of Nero\u2019s Roman chariot racecourse. At halftime, Romans killed Christians for entertainment. Whether forcing them to fight with wild animals or gladiators or being crucified, Romans 